# Minimal validation example for FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF, FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
# with FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C TRUE -- the ADAM orbital-rotation sub-loop builds its generalized Fock
# (and, via a double-counting trace identity, its energy) directly from UKB AO integrals at the
# current orbitals, instead of a stored MO-basis two-electron tensor re-expressed in the rotated
# basis on every ADAM step. Watch the log for the automatic start-up cross-check
# ("FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C: max |UKB-direct gradient - stored-tensor gradient| = ..."), which should
# be ~machine precision. Compare the converged energy against
# lih_gnof_c4_full_optimization.inp's own C4_DHF result -- must match (same system, same
# functional, a different gradient/energy SOURCE for the orbital-rotation sub-loop only).
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
C4_SPINOR TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
FUNCTIONAL_DIRECT_4C TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
